/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_Workflows_Clean Clean
 * @ingroup Foundation_Workflows_Development
 * @brief Remove known build and optional distribution directories safely.
 *
 * Cleanup always requires either an explicit preset or the explicit all flag.
 * Distribution outputs are retained unless their separate flag is supplied.
 * Clean does not modify source files, presets, toolchains, or files outside the
 * repository's `build/` and `dist/` roots.
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowCleanBash Bash
 *
 * @code{bash}
 * ./scripts/clean.sh <preset> [--dist]
 * ./scripts/clean.sh --all [--dist]
 *
 * ./scripts/clean.sh macos_arm64
 * ./scripts/clean.sh macos_arm64 --dist
 * ./scripts/clean.sh --all --dist
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowCleanPowerShell PowerShell
 *
 * @code{powershell}
 * ./scripts/clean.ps1 <preset> [-Dist]
 * ./scripts/clean.ps1 -All [-Dist]
 * @endcode
 *
 * Preset names are validated before they are used as paths. Cleanup is limited
 * to the repository's fixed `build/` and `dist/` roots; path traversal and
 * ambiguous no-argument cleanup are rejected.
 *
 * @section FoundationWorkflowCleanScope Scope
 *
 * | Command | Removes |
 * | --- | --- |
 * | `clean <preset>` | `build/<preset>` only |
 * | `clean <preset> --dist` / `-Dist` | Build and distribution for one preset |
 * | `clean --all` / `-All` | Entire `build/` tree only |
 * | `clean --all --dist` / `-All -Dist` | Entire `build/` and `dist/` trees |
 *
 * Use per-preset cleanup during normal work. All-target cleanup discards every
 * configured cache and can make multi-platform validation unnecessarily slow.
 * Export already refreshes its default distribution directory, so cleaning dist
 * first is useful for an explicit end-to-end test but is not required for every
 * export.
 */
